#
# This is the one Scoutro tool that is not a thin API client: prospect
# discovery needs several API calls (search + crawl) plus a filter and a small
# persistent state. It still uses only the public Scoutro API - no YaCy core
# change and no extra service.
#
# Pipeline:
#   DISCOVERY (Freeworld live search) -> FILTER -> ACCEPTED DOMAIN
#     -> safety/robots pre-check -> crawl.start with collection=prospect-<profile>
#
# Only the search index/text/metadata are kept: the Scoutro API crawls are
# text-only (storeHTCache/storeTXCache/media off, see the Olares package).
#
# Configuration (environment):
#   SCOUTRO_URL            base URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8090
#   SCOUTRO_USER           administrator user, default admin
#   SCOUTRO_PASSWORD       administrator password, or
#   SCOUTRO_PASSWORD_FILE  file containing the password (first line)
#   SCOUTRO_DISCOVERY_DIR  state directory, default ~/.scoutro-discovery
#
# Usage:
#   scoutro-discovery status
#   scoutro-discovery start [--profile P] [--dry-run] [--max-domains N]
#   scoutro-discovery pause | resume
#   scoutro-discovery search --profile P --query "Pflegeheim Koeln"
#   scoutro-discovery selftest

